Z||000000||Groot||08-20-99||07:12 AM||||Hi,<p>It seems i have a alternator in my 2.5L<br>that was meant for the V6 .....<br>Could that be the cause of my voltage<br>being 16 V or more ??<p>On my alternator it reads :<p>1100-507-Y94A<br>D193 12V NEG
Z||000001||theogre||08-20-99||08:04 AM||||No, that won't make the voltage be off.<p>first of all, if you are reading that on a dash gauge...... it could be wrong. test it across the batery terminals.<p>make sure everything is tight. a loos cable can cause this. getting above 15V is getting high. 18 is a problem.<p>after that have the alternator tested on a bench machine.
Z||000002||Bill 88||08-20-99||08:26 AM||||Previously, when the voltage got that high,(18) the problem was with the regulator.  This was on other cars that I have owned.  I am not sure with the Fiero's  
Z||000003||DJRice||08-20-99||01:43 PM||||I just had to deal with an overzealous alternator in my Buick.  It seems that a jump start after I had left my lights on at work caused the death of a diode in my regulator.  <br>Anyway, I drove with it overcharging for a couple of days.....and I ended up ruining the battery.  Its a good thing that battery was less than a year old, because I got a new one for nothing....
Z||000004||Groot||08-22-99||06:30 AM||||Thanx for all responses.<p>I figure indeed the alternator itself is<br>defective. Is the regulator built-in ?<br>Why is there a plug going into the<br>alternator ( red/black wire ) Is that<br>regulating voltage or just power supplied<br>to the internal regulator ??<p>By the way i measured the voltage over<br>the battery itself as i hoped first<br>the gauge in the car was inprecise.<br>Unfortunately ....<p>
Z||000005||theogre||08-22-99||02:50 PM||||pull it off and have it tested. that will eliminate any wiring problems in the car.
